    question: "Explain B-tree index bloat, fragmentation, and REINDEX strategies.",
    answer: "## Interview Answer\nNon-HOT updates and deletes leave empty index entries until vacuum reclaims — pages may stay allocated causing bloat. REINDEX rebuilds compact structure. REINDEX CONCURRENTLY (PG 12+) avoids long exclusive locks. pgstatuple and pgstattuple_approx measure bloat.\n\n## Detailed Explanation\nIndex bloat increases cache pressure and scan cost. VACUUM reclaims dead tuples but may not shrink index pages — REINDEX needed. REINDEX INDEX CONCURRENTLY builds new index, swaps via catalog update. pg_repack can rebuild indexes online too. autovacuum on index same as heap.\n\n## Production Perspective\nusers_email_idx bloated to 4GB (actual 800MB data) after bulk email update campaign. REINDEX INDEX CONCURRENTLY users_email_idx during low traffic; size 900MB, lookup latency halved.\n\n## Common Follow-up Questions\n• pg_repack vs REINDEX CONCURRENTLY?\n• Index bloat without heap bloat possible?\n• REINDEX on PK constraint index?\n• pgstatuple index scan safety?\n\n## Common Mistakes\n• REINDEX without CONCURRENTLY on production OLTP\n• Ignoring index bloat focusing only heap pgstattuple\n• REINDEX entire database during peak\n• Not investigating update pattern causing bloat\n\n## Senior Engineer Insights\nidx_scan high + idx_blks_read rising + index size growing = bloat suspicion before pgstattuple confirms.\n\n## Key Commands\n• CREATE EXTENSION pgstattuple;\n• SELECT * FROM pgstattuple('users_email_idx');\n• REINDEX INDEX CONCURRENTLY users_email_idx;\n• SELECT pg_size_pretty(pg_relation_size('users_email_idx'));\n\n## Best Practices\n• Monitor index size growth rate vs table growth\n• Use REINDEX CONCURRENTLY in maintenance windows\n• Fix HOT-unfriendly update patterns at source\n• Schedule bloat checks on top 20 indexes quarterly",
    command: "CREATE EXTENSION pgstattuple;\nSELECT * FROM pgstattuple('users_email_idx');\nREINDEX INDEX CONCURRENTLY users_email_idx;\nSELECT pg_size_pretty(pg_relation_size('users_email_idx'));",
    tags: ["postgresql","btree-index","medium","common"],
